  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), the loop calls array.IsNull(i) for each slot before validating union type codes/offsets. For malformed IPC input, a UnionArray can carry an invalid/null bitmap pointer-state (e.g., nonzero/unknown null count with missing or corrupted bitmap), and IsNull() unconditionally dereferences null_bitmap_data_ via BitUtil::GetBit when the pointer is non-null, leading to an out-of-bounds/invalid read and SEGV. The bug is missing structural validation of null bitmap presence/size/consistency before per-element null checks in UnionArray full validation.",
    "conditions": "Trigger via arrow-ipc-stream-fuzz by supplying a crafted IPC stream that decodes into a RecordBatch containing a UnionArray with inconsistent nullability metadata/buffers. FuzzIpcStream() opens the stream and calls RecordBatch::ValidateFull(); ValidateArrayData() dispatches to UnionArray visitor, which iterates length and invokes IsNull(i). With attacker-controlled malformed bitmap state, GetBit reads from invalid address and crashes."
  },
